{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_58","type":"agent_message","text":"\n\nThe task is complete. Here's what was accomplished:\n\n**Vulnerability Analysis**\n- The export-path traversal bug was in `repo/export_api/storage.py`\n- The `_normalize_requested_path` function only performed a single `unquote()`, allowing double-encoded payloads like `%252e%252e%252fsecrets.csv` to bypass checks\n\n**Fix Implemented** (`repo/export_api/storage.py`)\n- Added iterative unquoting loop that decodes until stable (handles double/triple encoding)\n- Added check for `..` path components after full normalization\n- Added rejection of Windows drive-qualified paths (e.g., `C:\\`)\n- Kept the existing tenant root containment check\n\n**Artifacts Created**\n- `audit/triage_note.json` - Documents SARIF-PY-TRAVERSAL-001 and APPSEC-EXP-17 as fixed\n- `repo/ops/deploy_hotfix.json` - Deployment instructions with verification steps and behavior claims\n\n**Validation**\n- `make test` - All 4 tests pass\n- `python3 bin/cnb55-hotfix-artifacts validate` - Both JSON artifacts validated successfully\n\nThe fix is minimal and targeted, only modifying `storage.py` without touching auth, dependencies, or unrelated config."}}
